   "id": "132d8806",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1. Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project builds a multiclass Network Intrusion Detection System using machine learning. The goal is to distinguish between normal traffic and multiple attack categories using network traffic features.\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7033c10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2. Import Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook uses pandas, NumPy, matplotlib, seaborn, scikit-learn, and imbalanced-learn for data preparation, modeling, and evaluation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "2da0a8f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Machine learning workflow components\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, classification_report\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
    "\n",
    "# Style setting for cleaner visual outputs in notebooks\n",
    "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5cf61e4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. Load Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is distributed across multiple CSV files, one per attack family. These are combined into a single training dataset before model development."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "6a68e4d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_dir = Path(\"../data\")\n",
    "\n",
    "attack_back = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back.csv\")\n",
    "bufferoverflow = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_BufferOverflow.csv\")\n",
    "FTPWrite = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_FTPWrite.csv\")\n",
    "guessPassword = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_GuessPassword.csv\")\n",
    "neptune = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_Neptune.csv\")\n",
    "NMap = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_NMap.csv\")\n",
    "normal = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_Normal.csv\")\n",
    "portsweep = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_PortSweep.csv\")\n",
    "rootkit = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_RootKit.csv\")\n",
    "satan = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_Satan.csv\")\n",
    "smurf = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_Smurf.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Align the FTPWrite dataset columns with the other attack files before concatenation\n",
    "cols = bufferoverflow.columns.tolist()\n",
    "FTPWrite = pd.read_csv(data_dir / \"Data_of_Attack_Back_FTPWrite.csv\", header=None, names=cols)"
   ]
  },
