    "# 13. Model Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "The most informative comparison for this imbalanced multiclass task is based on Macro F1. The table below reflects the project's recorded results without changing the original values.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Macro F1 |\n",
    "| --- | ---: |\n",
    "| Logistic Regression (without SMOTE) | 0.8093006359530651 |\n",
    "| Decision Tree (without SMOTE) | 0.7858146521904007 |\n",
    "| Random Forest (without SMOTE) | 0.8548396920033903 |\n",
    "| Logistic Regression + SMOTE | 0.7585572188279205 |\n",
    "| Decision Tree + SMOTE | 0.8553752163044486 |\n",
    "| Random Forest + SMOTE | 0.8005405883198035 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The strongest recorded Macro F1 in the original notebook was achieved by Decision Tree + SMOTE, while Random Forest without SMOTE was also very competitive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c104c74e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Some classes have very small support in the test set, particularly ftp_write, rootkit, and buffer_overflow. As a result, their per-class precision, recall, and F1 values can be unstable even when the overall macro metrics look strong."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "43f71a3d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 14. Final Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Random Forest + SMOTE was selected as the final model for this project based on the combination of Macro F1 and Macro Precision. Decision Tree + SMOTE achieved the same Macro F1 score, but the Random Forest model provided a stronger macro precision score in the recorded results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "825c91ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 15. Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates a practical multiclass intrusion detection workflow using a realistic, imbalanced cyber-attack dataset. The final workflow uses a proper train/test split, scaling fit on the training data only, and SMOTE applied only to the training data. This helps prevent information leakage and provides a more realistic estimate of model performance."
   ]
  }
